Junit5 Assertions:

-Assertions are used to verify expected outcomes in test

-if an assertion fails, the test faisls



1.assertEquals():

-checks if two values are equal or not
-if expected and actual value matches, test case is considered PASS



class MyServiceTest{
	
	@Test
	void testAddition(){
		
		//arrange
		MyService obj=new MyService();
		
		//act
		int output=obj.multiply(5,6);
		
		//assert
		assertEquals(30,output,"both are not equal");
	}
}



for primitive values it uses "==" and for objects it uses ".equals()"
---------------------------------------------------------------------


@Test
void testAssertEqualsForObject(){
	assertEquals("hello",new String("hello"));
}




String class, do overrides "equals" method, where it compares sequence of characters



so,if you are comparing custom objects, then do override "equals" and "hashCode" method in your class
else
Default "equals" method from Object class will be used.which checks for reference equality means, 2 different object with same value won't be considered same





